2026-09-02T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2185) 'Every part gets a stable OID under `1.3.6.1.4.1.66606.<arc>.parts.<hierarchy>`. Hierarchical addressing: `body/head/hair/front-fringe`, so a v4 addition is a new child, not a schema break.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2185  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2185) 'RFD66606-2183 (layer-decomp pipeline; V3 stopgap sits under this), RFD66606-2184 (EditScore bootstrap for unmapped parts), RFD66606-1122 (AlternativeTopology; reference precedent), RFD66606-1000 (RFD conventions; OID arc rules).
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2185  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2185) 'Leaf alias sets
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2185  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2185) 'Four leaf alias sets pointing at the same OID hierarchy: See-Through V3 (RFD66606-2183 stopgap), ANNY 104 joints (RFD66606-1122 topology), PASCAL-Part (public benchmark interop), VRM 1.0 humanoid bones (deployment interop). Ingest maps any leaf alias to the canonical OID; storage is OID, not string, so v3->v4 never rewrites a corpus.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2185  1 LINE
 Text:Written

